{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '685,774p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '1005,1115p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '80,160p' paper_strategy.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '685,774p' task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '1005,1115p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '80,160p' paper_strategy.md\"","aggregated_output":"def split_case(case, seed, smoke):\n    import numpy as np\n    groups = case['groups']\n    unique = sorted(set(groups), key=lambda group: hashlib.sha256(f'{seed}:{group}'.encode()).digest())\n    cut = min(len(unique) - 1, max(3, round(.7 * len(unique))))\n    source_set = set(unique[:cut])\n    source = np.asarray([index for index, group in enumerate(groups) if group in source_set])\n    target = np.asarray([index for index, group in enumerate(groups) if group not in source_set])\n    if smoke:\n        source = np.asarray(sorted(source, key=lambda index: (list(sorted(source_set)).index(groups[index]), int(index))))\n        order = []\n        for level in range(24):\n            for group in sorted(source_set):\n                matches = [index for index in source if groups[index] == group]\n                if level < len(matches):\n                    order.append(matches[level])\n        source = np.asarray(order[:24])\n        target = target[:4]\n    if len(source) < 6 or len(target) < 2:\n        raise ValueError('insufficient model split')\n    source_groups = [groups[index] for index in source]\n    if len(set(source_groups)) < 3:\n        raise ValueError('insufficient source calibration groups')\n    return case['matrix'][source], case['matrix'][target], source_groups, [groups[index] for index in target]\n\n\ndef anchor_baseline(source, target, budget, seed):\n    import numpy as np\n    from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n    vectors = source.astype(float).T\n    vectors -= vectors.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    norms = np.linalg.norm(vectors, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    vectors /= np.maximum(norms, 1e-8)\n    clusters = KMeans(n_clusters=budget, random_state=seed, n_init=1, max_iter=30).fit(vectors)\n    representatives = []\n    for center in clusters.cluster_centers_:\n        distance = np.sum((vectors - center) ** 2, axis=1)\n        distance[representatives] = np.inf\n        representatives.append(int(np.argmin(distance)))\n    distances = np.stack([np.sum((vectors - vectors[index]) ** 2, axis=1) for index in representatives], axis=1)\n    assignment = np.argmin(distances, axis=1)\n    weights = np.bincount(assignment, minlength=budget) / len(vectors)\n    if len(set(representatives)) != budget or not np.isclose(weights.sum(), 1):\n        raise RuntimeError('invalid anchor baseline')\n    return target[:, representatives] @ weights\n\n\ndef irt_baseline(source, target):\n    import numpy as np\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\n    from scipy.special import expit, logit\n    source = source.astype(float)\n    rows, columns = source.shape\n    initial_theta = logit(np.clip(source.mean(axis=1), .02, .98))\n    initial_theta = (initial_theta - initial_theta.mean()) / max(initial_theta.std(), .1)\n    initial = np.concatenate((initial_theta, np.zeros(columns), -logit(np.clip(source.mean(axis=0), .02, .98))))\n\n    def objective(parameters):\n        theta = parameters[:rows]\n        log_discrimination = parameters[rows:rows + columns]\n        discrimination = np.exp(log_discrimination)\n        difficulty = parameters[rows + columns:]\n        logits = theta[:, None] * discrimination - difficulty\n        residual = expit(logits) - source\n        loss = np.sum(np.logaddexp(0, logits) - source * logits) + .5 * np.sum(theta ** 2) + .05 * np.sum(log_discrimination ** 2) + .005 * np.sum(difficulty ** 2)\n        gradient = np.concatenate((residual @ discrimination + theta, np.sum(residual * theta[:, None], axis=0) * discrimination + .1 * log_discrimination, -residual.sum(axis=0) + .01 * difficulty))\n        return float(loss), gradient\n\n    fitted = minimize(objective, initial, method='L-BFGS-B', jac=True, bounds=[(-6, 6)] * rows + [(-3, 2)] * columns + [(-8, 8)] * columns, options={'maxiter': 40, 'maxls': 20, 'ftol': 1e-7})\n    if not np.isfinite(fitted.x).all() or fitted.fun > objective(initial)[0] + 1e-7:\n        raise RuntimeError('invalid IRT solver result')\n    discrimination = np.exp(fitted.x[rows:rows + columns])\n    difficulty = fitted.x[rows + columns:]\n    probability = expit(-difficulty)\n    order = np.argsort(-(discrimination ** 2 * probability * (1 - probability)), kind='stable')[:32]\n    predictions = []\n    for budget in BUDGETS:\n        selected = order[:budget]\n        answers = target[:, selected]\n        ability = np.zeros(len(target))\n        for step in range(30):\n            probability = expit(ability[:, None] * discrimination[selected] - difficulty[selected])\n            gradient = ((probability - answers) * discrimination[selected]).sum(axis=1) + ability\n            hessian = (probability * (1 - probability) * discrimination[selected] ** 2).sum(axis=1) + 1\n            ability = np.clip(ability - np.clip(gradient / hessian, -1, 1), -6, 6)\n        predictions.append(expit(ability[:, None] * discrimination - difficulty).mean(axis=1))\n    return np.asarray(predictions)\n\n\ndef baseline_worker():\ndef aggregate(episodes, outcomes, investigation):\n    import numpy as np\n    cases = list(investigation.cases)\n    seeds = SEEDS[:1] if investigation.smoke else SEEDS\n    families = sorted({investigation.cases[name]['family'] for name in cases})\n    weights = {name: 1 / len(families) / sum(investigation.cases[other]['family'] == investigation.cases[name]['family'] for other in cases) for name in cases}\n    records = {(episode['case'], episode['seed'], episode['condition']): outcome for episode, outcome in zip(episodes[:-1], outcomes[:-1])}\n\n    def mean_condition(condition, metric):\n        return sum(weights[name] / len(seeds) * records[name, seed, condition][metric] for name in cases for seed in seeds)\n\n    metrics = {name: 1.0 for name in METRICS}\n    for metric in ('mae', 'rmse', 'spearman', 'kendall_tau_b'):\n        metrics[metric] = mean_condition('primary', metric)\n    metrics['combined_score'] = 1 - metrics['mae']\n    for condition in CONDITIONS[1:]:\n        metrics[condition + '_mae'] = mean_condition(condition, 'mae')\n    deltas = {}\n    paired = True\n    for method in ('uniform', 'source_mean', 'anchor', 'irt'):\n        value = 0.0\n        for name in cases:\n            for seed in seeds:\n                baseline = investigation.baselines.get((name, seed))\n                truth = investigation.pairs[name, seed][1].mean(axis=1)\n                error = 1.0 if baseline is None else float(np.abs(baseline[method] - truth).mean())\n                value += weights[name] / len(seeds) * error\n                if method == 'anchor':\n                    primary = records[name, seed, 'primary']\n                    if baseline is None or primary['predictions'] is None:\n                        paired = False\n                        deltas[name, seed] = None\n                    else:\n                        deltas[name, seed] = (np.abs(primary['predictions'] - truth) - np.abs(baseline[method] - truth)).mean(axis=0)\n        metrics[method + '_mae'] = value\n    metrics['delta_anchor_mae'] = float(sum(weights[name] / len(seeds) * (1.0 if deltas[name, seed] is None else deltas[name, seed].mean()) for name in cases for seed in seeds))\n    metrics['delta_anchor_ci_low'], metrics['delta_anchor_ci_high'] = -1.0, 1.0\n    if paired:\n        random = np.random.default_rng(1729)\n        lineages = sorted({group for pair in investigation.pairs.values() for group in pair[3]})\n        draws = []\n        for repeat in range(1000):\n            seed_indices = random.integers(0, len(seeds), len(seeds))\n            counts = np.bincount(random.integers(0, len(lineages), len(lineages)), minlength=len(lineages))\n            value = 0.0\n            supported = True\n            for name in cases:\n                for seed_index in seed_indices:\n                    seed = seeds[int(seed_index)]\n                    multipliers = np.asarray([counts[lineages.index(group)] for group in investigation.pairs[name, seed][3]])\n                    if multipliers.sum() == 0:\n                        supported = False\n                        break\n                    value += weights[name] / len(seeds) * float(np.average(deltas[name, seed], weights=multipliers))\n            if not supported:\n                draws = []\n                break\n            draws.append(value)\n        if draws:\n            metrics['delta_anchor_ci_low'], metrics['delta_anchor_ci_high'] = map(float, np.quantile(draws, [.025, .975]))\n    replay = outcomes[-1]\n    first = outcomes[0]\n    reset_error = 1.0\n    if replay['success'] and first['success'] and replay['anchors'] == first['anchors']:\n        reset_error = float(np.max(np.abs(replay['predictions'] - first['predictions'])))\n    metrics['reset_mae'] = replay['mae']\n    metrics['reset_max_abs_error'] = reset_error\n    metrics['control_failure_rate'] = (sum(mean_condition(condition, 'control_failure') for condition in ('constant', 'copy', 'permuted')) + float(reset_error > 1e-10)) / 4\n    metrics['missing_episode_rate'] = sum(not outcome['success'] for outcome in outcomes) / len(episodes)\n    correct = all(outcome['success'] and outcome['control_failure'] == 0 for outcome in outcomes) and reset_error <= 1e-10 and investigation.baseline_complete and all(investigation.baselines.get((name, seed)) is not None for name in cases for seed in seeds)\n    metrics['correct'] = int(correct)\n    if set(metrics) != set(METRICS) or not all(type(value) in (int, float) and math.isfinite(value) for value in metrics.values()):\n        raise ValueError('invalid aggregate metrics')\n    evidence = []\n    for seed in seeds:\n        selected = [(episode, outcome) for episode, outcome in zip(episodes, outcomes) if episode['seed'] == seed]\n        seed_mae = sum(weights[name] * records[name, seed, 'primary']['mae'] for name in cases)\n        evidence.append({'seed': seed, 'score': 1 - seed_mae, 'correct': bool(all(outcome['success'] and outcome['control_failure'] == 0 for episode, outcome in selected) and reset_error <= 1e-10 and investigation.baseline_complete), 'duration_seconds': float(sum(outcome['duration'] for episode, outcome in selected))})\n        if PLANE == 'final':\n            solutions = {}\n            for name in cases:\n                baseline = investigation.baselines.get((name, seed))\n                conditions = {}\n                for episode, outcome in selected:\n                    if episode['case'] != name:\n                        continue\n                    condition = 'reset_replay' if episode.get('replay') else episode['condition']\n                    conditions[condition] = {'completed': outcome['success'], 'anchors': outcome['anchors'], 'predictions': None if outcome['predictions'] is None else outcome['predictions'].tolist(), 'mae': outcome['mae'], 'rmse': outcome['rmse'], 'spearman': outcome['spearman'], 'kendall_tau_b': outcome['kendall_tau_b'], 'structural_failure': outcome['control_failure'], 'duration_seconds': outcome['duration']}\n                solutions[name] = {'target_full_means': investigation.pairs[name, seed][1].mean(axis=1).tolist(), 'target_lineages': investigation.pairs[name, seed][3], 'conditions': conditions, 'baseline_predictions': None if baseline is None else {method: value.tolist() for method, value in baseline.items()}, 'baseline_failure_mae': 1.0 if baseline is None else None}\n            evidence[-1]['solution'] = {'budgets': list(BUDGETS), 'fixed_item_universes': True, 'cases': solutions}\n    return metrics, bool(correct), {'schema_version': 1, 'episodes': evidence}\n\n\ndef write_results(directory, metrics, correct, feasible, evidence=None):\n    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (directory / 'metrics.json').write_bytes(bounded_json_line(metrics))\n    (directory / 'correct.json').write_bytes(bounded_json_line({'correct': bool(correct)}))\n    if evidence is not None:\n        (directory / 'evaluation_evidence.json').write_bytes(bounded_json_line(evidence, 16 * 1024 * 1024))\n    if os.environ.get('AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION') == '1':\n        (directory / 'qualification.json').write_bytes(bounded_json_line({'schema_version': 1, 'feasible': bool(feasible)}))\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--program_path', required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--results_dir', required=True)\n    arguments = parser.parse_args()\n    directory = Path(arguments.results_dir)\n    smoke = os.environ.get('AGENTIC_TASK_DRAFT_SMOKE') == '1'\n    ceiling = 118 if smoke else WALL_SECONDS\n{\n  \"$id\": \"https://schemas.agentic-scientist.local/scientific-evidence/artifact-manifest.schema.json\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"artifact\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"id\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"source\",\n            \"derived\",\n            \"manuscript\",\n            \"figure\",\n            \"table\",\n            \"script\",\n            \"log\",\n            \"other\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"media_type\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"description\": \"Path to the artifact relative to the scientific-evidence root when possible.\",\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"sha256\": {\n          \"description\": \"Optional hash recorded when the producing workflow computes one.\",\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"path\",\n        \"kind\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"derived_from\": {\n      \"description\": \"Inline @evidence refs or stable ids describing the artifact inputs.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"minLength\": 1,\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"generated_by\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"command\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"minLength\": 1,\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"minItems\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"cwd\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"finished_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_path\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"script_sha256\": {\n          \"pattern\": \"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"started_at\": {\n          \"format\": \"date-time\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"script_path\"\n      ],\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"named_outputs\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": [\n          \"string\",\n          \"number\",\n          \"integer\",\n          \"boolean\",\n          \"array\",\n          \"object\",\n          \"null\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional machine-readable outputs emitted by the derivation.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"schema_name\": {\n      \"const\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"schema_name\",\n    \"artifact\",\n    \"derived_from\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Scientific Evidence Artifact Manifest\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n2. Show a compact table of **recorded final aggregates**, explicitly labeled as including worst-case defaults where outputs are missing.\n3. Compare **available matched predictions** by benchmark, then examine budget and ranking behavior under the same stated support rule.\n4. Interpret heterogeneity and the evidence boundary, without turning conditional analyses into a repaired or qualified evaluation.\n\nThe aggregate table can include these recorded values:\n\n| Condition | Recorded aggregate MAE | Grounding source |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Studied estimator | 0.08801465854359276 | `final.metric.mae` |\n| Uniform selection with fitted prediction | 0.044910877034389785 | `final.metric.no_diversity_mae` |\n| Selected-item observed mean | 0.10836174574059959 | `final.metric.no_calibration_mae` |\n| Uniform-item sample mean | 0.1335974367939037 | `final.metric.uniform_mae` |\n| IRT reference | 0.1186668212839868 | `final.metric.irt_mae` |\n| Anchor reference | 0.22047382735923254 | `final.metric.anchor_mae` |\n\nThese are **not** a pure measured-accuracy leaderboard. In particular, the lower fitted-uniform aggregate does not demonstrate a causal selection advantage. Missing reference outputs are not measured baseline MAE of one.\n\nFor conditional figures, first determine support from availability and the relevant structural flags, not from favorable metric values. Use the common case-seed intersection across each figure's displayed methods and state retained and missing support. Recompute budget-specific errors and rank correlations from stored predictions and `target_full_means`, with deterministic scripts. Keep missing predictions null and preserve every failed record in the audit.\n\nWhen conditionally aggregating, retain equal source-domain weight, equal cases within domain, equal retained seeds within case, and equal checkpoints when averaging budgets. Explain the changed within-case support normalization. Do not silently drop an entire failed case, silently replace the official aggregate, or represent this conditioning as confirmatory validation.\n\nShow all three seeds where available; use clearly labeled descriptive ranges, not invented error bars. Seeds and models overlap, and fixed benchmarks are not independent benchmark/item-population samples. An informative paired interval is unavailable. Any later dependence-aware uncertainty calculation must be separately labeled exploratory, derived from actual records, and never guessed here.\n\nThe main-text audit must preserve the failed qualification and describe incomplete records and failed checks. A successful checked replay (`final.metric.reset_max_abs_error = 0.0`) does not validate every other requirement. Unverified candidate diagnostics are not independent evidence.\n\n## Required Figures and Readability Budgets\n\n### Template Geometry\n\nThe inspected `paper.sty` specifies **one text column, 5.5 inches wide and 9 inches high**. Thus ordinary column width and full text width coincide. Use regular single-column figures at `\\linewidth`; a `full_width` strategy label does not call for a two-column float. Treat the supplied style as the selected format artifact, not proof that official-template freshness has been independently checked.\n\n### Figure 1 — Method and Evidence Overview\n\n- **Purpose:** immediate glance value for the source-only design, target prefix, estimator, and distinction between prediction error and unavailable evidence.\n- **Generator:** `generate-concept-figure`; this is the only planned figure using that workflow.\n- **Placement/footprint:** page 1 or 2; full text width, approximately **5.5 × 1.9 inches**, plus caption.\n- **Content budget:** one diagram, at most six concise blocks arranged in two rows with no more than three blocks per row; at most three visual streams; final-size text at least **9 pt**.\n- **Layout justification:** the mechanism is not legible from scores alone. Two short rows at the actual single-column width explain information access without dense architecture artwork. Separate the optional particle and ridge branches; do not draw arrows implying demonstrated improvement.\n\n### Figure 2 — Available-Pair Method Comparison\n\n- **Purpose:** measured MAE across benchmarks for primary, fitted uniform selection, anchor and IRT, without plotting missing-record defaults as observations.\n- **Generator/type:** `matplotlib`, grouped horizontal dot plots.\n- **Placement/footprint:** full text width, approximately **5.5 × 3.8 inches**, plus caption; two vertically stacked source-domain panels.\n- **Readability budget:** two panels, one per row; four and six benchmark categories respectively; four method series maximum; final-size text at least **8.5 pt**.\n- **Implementation:** equal-budget average within each available matched seed; seed points plus an explicitly descriptive available-seed mean; common-support annotations; unavailable markers outside the numerical axis. Use one legend and a shared labeled linear scale.\n- **Layout justification:** full width leaves room for case labels and four methods; vertical stacking avoids squeezing six cases into a narrow panel. If scale separation hides useful comparisons, simplify/rework the plot and use its accompanying absolute-value table—do not shrink labels or suppress the original anchor reference.\n\n### Figure 3 — Item Budget, Error, and Ranking\n\n- **Purpose:** compare fitted reconstruction and raw response means under selected and uniform items, using both error and ranking quality.\n- **Generator/type:** `matplotlib`, grouped dot plots without development trajectories.\n- **Placement/footprint:** full text width, approximately **5.5 × 2.5 inches**, plus caption; two side-by-side panels for MAE and Spearman correlation.\n- **Readability budget:** two panels in one row, three budget categories each, four method series maximum; final-size text at least **8.5 pt**; one shared legend.\n- **Methods:** primary, fitted uniform selection, selected-item observed mean, uniform-item sample mean. Use identical available support across the displayed methods and both panels, and document conditional aggregation weights.\n- **Layout justification:** three categories permit readable approximately 2.6-inch panels. Distinct metric labels and directions prevent readers from conflating lower error and higher correlation. Budgets are experimental conditions, not search milestones. Do not assume monotonic behavior.\n\n### Main Tables and Export Rules\n\nKeep the aggregate/default-disclosure table and compact missing-record/structural-check audit next to the results, not solely in the supplement. Quantitative figures must export **vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI**, with LaTeX referencing the PDF whenever available. Keep source files and the editable overview. Raster-only full-width output must be regenerated at **at least 2400 px** wide; any later column-width raster-only output needs **at least 1200 px**. Never upscale existing rasters.\n\n## Body Layout: Substantive 8.5-Page Target\n\nICLR 2026 requires an anonymous **8–9-page body**, excluding references; an 8-page body qualifies for the layout requirement only when its final page is at least 75% full. Plan approximately:\n\n| Content | Body pages, including associated visuals |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Title, abstract, introduction, early overview | 1.4 |\n| Focused related work | 0.6 |\n| Problem, fixed-universe protocol, evidence mask | 1.3 |\n| Source-only design and prediction method | 1.7 |\n| Comparisons, budget/ranking results, aggregate and audit tables | 2.2 |\n| Discussion and limitations | 1.0 |\n| Conclusion | 0.3 |\n| **Target** | **8.5** |\n\nThese are planning allocations, not measured quantities. Spend available space on the estimator equations, comparator semantics, fixed-universe/grouped protocol, clear comparisons, uncertainty limits, and failure evidence. Do not pad with development branches, generic motivation, speculative experiments, or repeated caveats. Preserve enough main-text detail to understand the method and central limitations without the supplement.\n\nSuggested headings: **Introduction; Related Work; Fixed-Benchmark Score Prediction; Source-Only Item Design and Prediction; Evaluation Protocol and Evidence Availability; Prediction Error and Ranking on Available Pairs; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion.**\n\nOmit names, affiliations, acknowledgements, funding statements, identifying links and internal host paths. Include the required separate **LLM Usage** section after references if convenient. Do not invent a conference checklist requirement; check applicable submission requirements downstream.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
