{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_128","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-\\\\subsection{Availability Masks and Statistical Interpretation}\n+\\\\subsection{Seed-Level Records and Exhaustive Numerical Ledger}\n+Table~\\\\ref{tab:seed_si} gives the recorded primary metrics for every case--seed pair, averaged equally over budgets. The target count and number of recorded target-group labels vary with the split. A missing primary record stays missing in this table rather than inheriting its evaluator penalty. This table retains the affected rows explicitly, while the main aggregate table preserves the separately scored defaults.\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n+\n+\\\\begin{table}[p]\n+\\\\centering\\\\small\n+\\\\setlength{\\\\tabcolsep}{3pt}\n+\\\\caption{All primary case--seed records. \"'$T$ counts targets and $H$ their recorded groups. Errors and correlations average the three budgets. Missing outputs are not measured errors; available rows do not repair failed overall qualification.}\n+'\"\\\\label{tab:seed_si}\n+\\\\begin{tabular}{lrrrrrrr}\n+\\\\toprule\n+Case & Seed & \"'$T$ & $H$ & MAE & RMSE & Spearman & Kendall'\"\\\\\\\\\n+\\\\midrule\n+% BEGIN GENERATED primary_seed_metrics\n+% END GENERATED primary_seed_metrics\n+\\\\bottomrule\n+\\\\end{tabular}\n+\\\\end{table}\n+\n+An exhaustive machine-readable table, \\\\texttt{complete\\\\_metrics.csv}, additionally retains every recorded condition and reference, separated by case, seed, and budget. It includes primary, both fitted/raw-mean controls, matched constant/copied/permuted observations, replay where recorded, and anchor/IRT/uniform/source-mean references. Missing prediction metrics are blank, not penalty values; availability and structural-failure fields remain separate. Scores for a condition with a failed structural check describe its recorded output only, not validated performance. The table and its provenance sidecar are generated by the same transformation script as the figures.\n+% @evidence[[complete_metrics.csv]]\n+\n+For completeness, the remaining reported diagnostic MAEs are 0.2220 for constant observations, 0.1545 for copied observations, 0.1005 for permuted observations, and 0.0281 for replay. These evaluator summaries have their original weighting and scope; they are not new controlled accuracy estimates. In particular, replay covers the checked repeated case rather than the full benchmark collection, and matched corrupted observations are not ordinary target responses.\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/constant_mae]]\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/copy_mae]]\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/permuted_mae]]\n+% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/metrics/reset_mae]]\n+\n+\\\\subsection{Availability Masks and Statistical Interpretation}\n*** Update File: claims_grounding.json\n@@\n-    {\n-      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The evaluated source-only selector uses equal total group weights, empirical score covariance, diagonal nugget 0.1 max(mu(1-mu),0.05), and greedy squared conditional covariance divided by conditional item variance floored at 1e-12. It uses low-rank updates and no target-adaptive acquisition.\\\",\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"The supplementary seed table retains every primary case-seed record, recorded target/group counts, and budget-averaged MAE/RMSE/Spearman/Kendall. Missing rows remain missing. The exhaustive CSV separates each budget, condition and reference with availability/structural status.\\\",\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"citation_keys\\\": [],\n+      \\\"evidence_refs\\\": [\\\"@evidence[[tables/primary_seed_metrics.tex]]\\\", \\\"@evidence[[complete_metrics.csv]]\\\", \\\"@evidence[[build_paper_artifacts.py]]\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"claim\\\":